# Copy to `api/.env.local` for api values that are yours rather than the project's. Gitignored;
# this example is not.
#
#   cp api/.env.local.example api/.env.local
#
# This is the most specific file there is short of the environment itself, so anything set here
# wins over everything. Use it only for something that must not follow the repo-wide value -
# otherwise put it in `../.env.local`, which is the place most overrides belong and which carries
# the full precedence order.
#
# Every variable the api reads is listed with its committed default, so overriding one is
# uncommenting rather than going to look it up.

# ── secrets, which have no default ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Keys connector credentials are encrypted with, as a comma separated list of `id:base64` pairs.
# The first is the active one. Generate one with:
#
#   echo "k1:$(openssl rand -base64 32)"
#DIELE_SECRET_KEYS=

# Generated and printed at startup when unset. Set it to script an install.
#LOCAL_SETUP_TOKEN=

# ── sign-in ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# `local` keeps accounts here and signs them in with a password. `oidc` runs the authorization
# code flow and needs the values below it. `dev` grants every login as a fixed identity and
# belongs nowhere reachable by others.
#AUTH_MODE=local
#OIDC_ISSUER=https://sso.example.com/application/o/diele/
#OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
#OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
#OIDC_SCOPES="openid email profile"
#OIDC_DISPLAY_NAME="Single Sign-On"

# ── everything else the api reads ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Change VITE_API_TARGET in `../.env.local` to match, or the dev server proxies to the wrong
# place.
#PORT=3000

# Origin the browser reaches diele on. The OIDC redirect uri is derived from it.
#PUBLIC_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173

# Created and migrated on boot; delete the file to start over. A relative path is resolved from
# the repo root, so it lands in ./data/ whichever directory npm ran from.
#DB_PATH="data/diele.db"

# Whether a database created by this boot gets the search engines, slash commands and local ports
# every portal would hold anyway, most of them switched off. Read only while the schema is
# created, so turning it off later changes nothing that is already there.
#DIELE_SEED_STOCK_CONFIG="true"

# Idle windows rather than lifetimes: both roll forward on every use. The second is what
# `remember me` picks at login.
#SESSION_MAX_AGE_MS=86400000
#SESSION_REMEMBER_MAX_AGE_MS=7776000000

# Defaults to on when PUBLIC_ORIGIN is https and off otherwise, which is almost always right.
#SESSION_COOKIE_SECURE=false

# The wordmark, the line under it, and the accent. One accent value per theme, six-digit hex.
#BRAND_TITLE="diele"
#BRAND_SUBTITLE="start page"
#BRAND_ACCENT_LIGHT="#16a34a"
#BRAND_ACCENT_DARK="#22c55e"
